{"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"CollectorEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"CollectorEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"CollectorEncoding"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatch"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/SkippedRecord","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/collectorencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the "},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a self-hosted TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"POST \/v1\/batches","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Give it to an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") as its encoder,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and pass the collector’s API key to the destination as an "},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" header field."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is JSON: one object per record, with the record’s identifier (which a redelivered record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps), the event’s name, its timestamp, whether it is redelivered, its properties and its context.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Properties are read from the event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":" form, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" derives, through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. The context holds the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context keys the record has values for, its session and sample rate, and its trace context. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is written only while the record reveals it; once redacted, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property is left out, and an array’s element, or a value inside a type the plan can’t map, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one whose event and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"version the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one holding a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"JSON can’t, such as a NaN. Each is logged; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns the body","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with each record left out as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/SkippedRecord","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". When no record of a batch can be written,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/encode(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" throws, and the destination sends nothing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to a server of your own format, write a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of your own. To send to PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema])","let encoder = CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan)","let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com\/v1\/batches","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","    encoder: encoder)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sending to the collector beside the other destinations."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" to send."}],"references":{"do